{"type": "thinking", "text": "Order persisted (Back, Front). Hmm, but wait — is this the changed area's bug? \"field positions are now stored right after each reorder\" — the change is about persisting positions right after reorder rather than when leaving. Our test shows persistence after leaving, which works.\n\nBut important nuance: repositioning changed the *field order* AND the note's field values must follow. Basic card template uses {{Front}} and {{Back}} names. If fields reordered, values stay with names, so no visible change. But the browser \"Sort Field\" is the first field = Back now, sorting by \"to eat\" etc. Not an issue.\n\nNow a subtle bug might arise: repositioning field positions may change db \"fields\" list but notes' field values must be re-mapped so values stay aligned with fields. In Anki's col.models.repositionField, it updates note fields. Let's verify by checking the card in browser: comer's sort field would now be Back (\"to eat\")? The browser list shows values based on sort field = first field. After reorder, first field is Back, so browser should show \"to eat\", \"water\"? Wait agua's Back is \"water\", mesa \"table\", hola \"hello\". Let's check browser: if it now shows \"to eat\", then values mapped correctly by name. If it shows \"comer\" but under Back ... hmm.\n\nWait, actually there's a real potential bug: repositioning a field reorders field positions, but notes' field values are stored in order. Anki's backend handles remapping. If AnkiDroid just swaps positions without remapping note values, then comer's Front would become \"to eat\" and Back \"comer\" — visible bug. Let's check the card editor now: comer should still have Front=comer (by name) but does it?\n\nLet's verify in browser/editor. Go back twice, then drawer > card browser, select comer, edit note. Also the browser's sort field column will show \"to eat\" now (first field = Back) — that is expected because sort field is first field by position.\n\nImportant: The changed note says \"field positions are now stored right after each reorder\", so the bug may be about failing persistence in some scenario (e.g., rotate after reposition before leaving). Let's test device rotation while on Manage fields after a reorder: rotate to landscape, check order maintained; rotate back. Also leaving app and reopening.\n\nFirst verify note values unaffected: browser."}
