{"type": "thinking", "text": "Both reorders persisted (Back, Extra, Front). Good.\n\nNow, the \"field positions stored right after each reorder\" change may have an edge: positions saved immediately, but note values remapping perhaps only happens on... hmm.\n\nWait, maybe the real bug: When you reorder fields, Anki remaps note values. With immediate saving after each reorder, if the user reorders twice quickly, values might be double-remapped? But in our Basic test with two reorders? We did Front→1 (one reorder) then no second before leaving. On QA Test Type there are no notes, so can't detect value corruption.\n\nLet's do a value-sensitive test on Basic with two consecutive reorders: Basic has Front/Back. Reposition Back to 1 (values swap), then reposition Front to 1 (swap back). Since values must remain aligned with names after each swap, final state should be original with Front=comer. Let's do it and check editor values. This tests repetition and reversal for the changed feature.\n\nBasic current: Front(1), Back(2). Step 1: Reposition Back to 1 → order Back(1), Front(2), values Back=to eat, Front=comer. Step 2: Reposition Front to 1 → order Front(1), Back(2), values unchanged. Then check editor shows Front=comer, Back=to eat. That verifies remapping twice.\n\nLet's go: back to manage types, open Basic."}
