{"type": "thinking", "text": "Back, Extra, Front — correct. So reorder logic seems correct even for middle positions.\n\nHmm. So where's the injected bug in the note type field editor? Maybe in a different aspect: \"field positions are now stored right after each reorder\" — perhaps the bug is that the *sort field* indication changed? Or the note type's field positions in the DB but note fields not remapped when reordering on a type with notes... we tested values on Basic twice and fine.\n\nWait — maybe the bug is the reverse: previously positions were stored on leaving; now saved immediately. A side effect: after reorder, if you press \"Back\" (navigate up) -> the screen might save the OLD adapter order (overwriting the immediate save) because the adapter list wasn't updated? Our tests show persistence fine.\n\nMaybe the bug involves reordering during search/filter? No.\n\nMaybe the bug is: positions are stored right after each reorder, but the *note type's field list in the editor* uses 1-based positions while notes' `ord` are 0-based... but no visible issue.\n\nCould the bug be that repositioning doesn't refresh the card templates' field references? Not part of the change.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the bug is not in what I think; maybe the four \"changed\" items are hints about where bugs may be, and not all are buggy. The browser popup had one confirmed bug. Maybe only one bug exists. But likely there could be more (e.g., 2 bugs). Let's keep testing other aspects.\n\nLet me finish with note types: test field rename persistence and delete field + undo, and note type rename. Also \"Edit cards\" (card templates) route. But time/steps: we have plenty.\n\nActually, one thing to verify for \"field positions stored right after each reorder\": after reordering, if the app is killed/restarted without leaving the screen, positions should persist. We could test by pressing HOME then reopening the app (open_app brings to foreground without reset). Let's test: currently QA Order Type fields Back, Extra, Front. Press HOME, then open_app, see if state is preserved (activity restarted?). HOME then open_app likely resumes same activity. Not a strong test.\n\nAlternatively rotate device while on Manage fields after reorder — our earlier rotation was after restoring order; we tested landscape kept order. That's fine.\n\nMaybe check \"field positions\" in the DB via UI: the \"Sort by this field\" menu. Eh.\n\nLet me test rename field: rename Extra to \"ExtraRenamed\", verify persistence, then delete Extra, then rename back? Renaming and deleting is reversible. Actually deleting a field from a note type with 0 notes is safe.\n\nTest rename: tap Extra's menu → Rename field → \"Extra2\" → save → verify list & persistence."}
