{"type": "thinking", "text": "Data restored to 7 note types.\n\nNow regarding the note type field editor, I haven't found a bug. Let me think about whether there's a bug related to \"field positions stored right after each reorder\" visible in the UI. Maybe the \"Sort by this field\" behavior: after repositioning fields, the sort field should remain valid. Test setting sort field to a field then reordering. Hmm.\n\nWait — reconsider the changed statement: \"Note type field editor: field positions are now stored right after each reorder.\" Perhaps in the *previous* build positions were only stored when the screen was exited; the change stores after each reorder. The injected bug might be: the storage call passes the *new position* but uses `adapterPosition` incorrectly, e.g., after moving a field from 1 to 3, positions stored are wrong when there are 3+ fields and moving downward. Our test: Front(1) → 2 produced Back, Front, Extra (correct). Extra(3) → 2 produced Back, Extra, Front (correct). Hmm both correct.\n\nWhat about moving a field downward past multiple (1→3)? Test on a 3-field type: Front from 1 to 3 → expected Back, Extra, Front. We did the equivalent indirectly (Extra3→2 then...). Let's do a fresh 3-field type test with 1→3 move. Might reveal off-by-one when moving down more than one.\n\nAlso test 3→1 (done earlier on QA Test Type: Extra3→1 gave Extra, Front, Back correct).\n\nSo 1→3 is untested. Basic has only 2 fields; a 1→2 move works. In a 3-field type, 1→3 differs. Let me recreate the type quickly once more? That's several steps but doable.\n\nAlternatively, temporarily add a third field to Basic, do 1→3, check, then delete it and restore order. Adding/deleting a field on Basic is more invasive but reversible; deletion of field removes no data (new field empty). Risk: if the injected bug corrupts note values during reorder, we'd damage Basic notes — but we'd catch it and can revert? Actually if values get misassigned, restoring order would restore mapping. Probably fine. But safer with a temp type.\n\nI've already created two temp types; one more is fine. Let me do it.\n\nActually, wait. Before more note type testing, let me revisit the browser area more thoroughly, since that has the confirmed bug and maybe more. The browser changed item was the popup; maybe other browser stuff (browsing/editing) is fine. We tested edit note save/discard/persist, search, sort. Maybe test:\n- Editing tags (add/remove tag) and check filter by tag.\n- Change note type / change deck (not changed build though).\n- Card browser multiple selection bulk operations.\n- Preview.\n- Undo (edit) — undo after save to revert? We saved twice; undo available. Not necessary.\n\nLet me test tags editing since preconditions mention \"comer (tagged verb), no other tags exist\". Testing tag filtering already showed 1 card. Also editing tags via card editor Tags button. Let's test adding a tag then removing, verify.\n\nAlso check \"Filter by tag\" menu shows only \"verb\".\n\nBut first finish the note type 1→3 test. Hmm, balance. The note type area is a listed changed area; the injected bug may be there. I need to find it if exists. Let me do the 1→3 test.\n\nCreate type again: navigate to Manage note types (currently there). FAB → name \"QA Move Type\" → add → open fields → add Extra → reorder Front 1→3 → check order; then reorder Front 3→1 restore; check; then maybe test leaving persistence; delete type.\n\nLet's go."}
