{"type": "thinking", "text": "Cleaned up.\n\nNow let me re-examine the deck-list expand/collapse arrows area more thoroughly. The change: \"each arrow's touch target is now separated from the rest of the deck row.\" We tested that tapping arrow toggles and tapping row at x=140 opens deck. But potential bug: tapping the arrow also opens the deck when tapping the arrow's edge? We tested center of arrow and row. Also maybe tapping just left/right of arrow (e.g., x=100 or x=30) should still hit arrow? Not important.\n\nAnother potential bug: after expanding, the arrow direction icon changes; we saw Expand→Collapse. Good. What about rotated device with subdecks? Eh.\n\nBut maybe the injected bug: the arrow's touch target is separated, but now the row's clickable area is smaller so tapping the arrow no longer toggles? We saw it toggles. Hmm.\n\nAnother possibility: arrow overlap with the counts layout on the right? No.\n\nMaybe there's a bug where tapping the arrow of a collapsed deck with subdecks opens the deck instead of expanding (event not consumed)? Our test: tap expand → expanded, no navigation. Good.\n\nRe-test repeat: expand/collapse several times works.\n\nWhat about a deck with subdecks that has due cards? Not needed.\n\nLet's look at the deck retitling clash area more: potential injected bug: comparing text instead of identifiers might reject renaming a deck to its own name? Tested - allowed. Case-insensitive - blocked. Trailing space - blocked. What about renaming a *subdeck* to its own full name? Tested? We opened rename for Spanish::Sub1 and cancel/renamed Sub2. We didn't press Rename with unchanged name (Sub1). Let's test that: create subdeck, rename to same full name, should work. Hmm, earlier \"same name\" for top-level worked.\n\nAnother edge: rename a deck to \"French::Sub\" while \"French\" exists → allowed (no clash). But if there's an existing deck \"French::Sub1\", renaming to \"French::Sub1\" should clash. We didn't test cross-parent textual clash: e.g., rename Spanish to \"French\" (blocked, tested). What about rename Spanish to \"French::Sub1\" after creating? We deleted Sub1. Could recreate quickly and test clash with a subdeck's full name via a *different* deck's rename. E.g., create subdeck \"Sub1\" under Spanish; then try renaming French to \"Spanish::Sub1\" — should be flagged \"Name already exists\". If the clash check compares display text only (\"Sub1\") it might incorrectly flag something else, or if it compares only top-level names it may miss. Let's test: French → \"Spanish::Sub1\" should be blocked as an exact full-name match. Then also test French → \"Other::Sub1\" should be ALLOWED (different full name; display \"Sub1\" same as existing). If blocked, that's a bug (false positive from comparing display names). This is likely the injected bug: comparing text of the *displayed* name rather than full path. Hmm, but the change says \"comparing text instead of identifiers\" — the concept: previous code compared `deck.id` to known ids; new code compares name strings. A potential bug: comparing *display name* (last component) instead of full name.\n\nLet's test! Create subdeck Sub1 under Spanish, then rename French to \"Other::Sub1\".\nExpected: allowed (creates Other::Sub1). If \"Name already exists\" appears → bug (false clash due to display-name comparison).\n\nAlso test rename French → \"Spanish::Sub1\" → should block (full name exists).\n\nLet's do it. Currently on Manage note types. Navigate back to deck list."}
