{"type": "thinking", "text": "Cleaned up; Spanish/French only.\n\nNow back to the browser question about empty search. Let me decide whether to report. Also test editing tags. And maybe test the \"new-card ordering popup\" hint with a different locale? The bug found is enough for that.\n\nLet me also double-check the reposition dialog hint under French selection: hint top/bottom would be 1..7 still (collection-wide). Not needed.\n\nConsider the browser empty-search stale results. Let me test in a fresh sequence to be certain and decide:\n1. Browser (Spanish 4 cards).\n2. Search \"mesa\" → 1 card.\n3. Clear via X.\n4. Press IME Search (with empty field).\n5. Observe list still 1 card (mesa) and query empty.\n6. Close search bar → 4 cards.\n\nIs that a defect? Expected: searching empty query shows all cards. The UI clearly shows an empty search field while the list is filtered to one card — inconsistent. I think it's reportable as \"no_effect\"/\"wrong_value\". But the dev might say \"by design: empty search is ignored; clear search bar (X) closes filter only when submitted\". Hmm.\n\nActually wait: There's subtlety — the \"Clear query\" X button in AnkiDroid's SearchView might be a custom \"clear\" that both clears text and *submits empty*? Apparently not. In stock Android SearchView, the close button clears text but does not submit; pressing Enter submits. AnkiDroid's CardBrowser.onQueryTextSubmit with empty string... should show all. But maybe AnkiDroid explicitly ignores empty query to prevent showing whole collection? Hmm, in AnkiDroid card browser, an empty search shows all cards in current deck — that's the normal state. When you first open the browser, the search bar shows \"deck:Spanish\" prefilled? Here the search box was empty and list showed 4 cards, with toolbar \"Spanish | 4 cards shown\". So empty query = all deck cards.\n\nSo submitting empty should return to that state, and it didn't. But did my tap actually trigger submit? The IME \"Search\" key tap may not have been registered because the field had focus and the tap coordinates... The key element 35 was at (999,2194) — it should. After tapping, observe had no snackbar and same list. Hmm, but note: the snackbar \"1 card shown\" was present before and disappeared — likely just timed out after 4s. So can't conclude.\n\nMaybe the app didn't get the IME action because type_text's submit earlier worked via key event; tapping the IME button sends a key event too. Should work.\n\nLet me test again more explicitly with a different query: search \"hola\" (list 1 card), clear X, then instead of IME key, press the hardware/keyboard ENTER using press_key ENTER (we tried earlier and it didn't refresh either). Hmm, both failed.\n\nI could also try tapping elsewhere to dismiss keyboard? Hmm.\n\nGiven the risk, maybe test whether empty search *except via closing bar* is intended by trying to search from scratch: open search bar with empty field (freshly opened), press IME Search — what's the result? If it does nothing (list stays 4 cards), then \"empty submit is ignored\" is consistent design (no change since list already all). That wouldn't distinguish.\n\nActually, if empty submit were handled, after clearing it would show 4 cards. It didn't. The bar has a \"Search all decks\" action; not relevant.\n\nIs this related to the changed build? No. The task says sweep the areas; bugs in those areas count regardless of changes. A stale list vs empty query is a consistency bug. But if it's long-standing intended behavior, reporting wastes a report (but not fatal? The instruction says a confirmed report is logged; maybe false reports penalized). I'd rather be conservative but this seems like a genuine UX bug.\n\nHmm, let me look for stronger evidence: after clearing text with X, does the toolbar still say \"1 card shown\" snackbar (it did). Then pressing the IME search showed no snackbar. If submit had happened with empty query, AnkiDroid would show snackbar \"4 cards shown\" (we saw \"4 cards shown\" snackbars after edits). So no submit occurred. So the Search action with empty text is being ignored by the IME/app. Is the IME action listener disabled when text empty? In Android, `setOnQueryTextListener` still receives empty strings.\n\nMaybe AnkiDroid's code: `if (query.isEmpty() && !isSearchViewExpanded) ...`. Hmm.\n\nLet me try pressing the IME Search key twice? Or press ENTER via type_text submit on empty (submit=true with empty text)? type_text with submit triggers IME action. We did press_key ENTER once.\n\nI'll try one more time: open search, type \"hola\", submit, clear X, then use type_text with text \"\" submit=true into field. See if list refreshes. If not, report as bug? Let me also test the same in French deck maybe.\n\nActually, thinking about it more: I recall AnkiDroid's card browser saves the search query in the deck's \"search\" state; clearing the search bar and pressing search should show all. I'm fairly confident this is a real bug (Search action ignored when query empty). Hmm, but is it in scope? \"browsing and editing cards\" — yes, search is browsing.\n\nBut wait: maybe the requirement is that the X clear button is *supposed* to immediately clear the search (i.e., it should show all). It didn't — that alone is a bug? Actually in stock SearchView, X just clears text; the query remains until submit/close. Then submitting empty should work.\n\nRisk assessment: If I report and dev rejects, it's a wasted report but the session continues. The dev replies quickly with confirm/reject. I think it's worth one more careful reproduction. Let me do it now.\n\nSteps: from deck list, open browser, search \"hola\" (submit), clear X, then tap IME Search. Check."}
