{"type": "text", "text": "The device bridge dropped (persistent `BrokenPipeError`) before I could sign off, but here's my completed sweep summary.\n\n## Bug found (confirmed & logged)\n\n**Reposition new cards dialog — duplicated range hint label**\n- Screen: Card browser → overflow → Reposition (dialog titled \"Reposition new cards\")\n- Observed: `Queue top: ⁨1⁩\\nQueue top: ⁨7⁩`\n- Expected: two distinct bounds, e.g. \"Queue top: 1\" / \"Queue bottom: 7\"\n- Steps: Card browser → Select all → overflow → Reposition, read the hint above Starting position / Step. Reproduced twice; developer confirmed and logged it.\n\n## Areas covered (no further defects confirmed)\n\n**Deck management**\n- Rename clash: exact name (\"French\" for Spanish) → \"Name already exists\", Rename disabled; case-insensitive (\"french\") and trailing-space (\"French \") also caught; subdeck full path (\"Spanish::Sub1\") caught; same displayed sub-name under a different parent (\"Other::Sub1\") correctly allowed; renaming to own current name allowed; empty name disabled; Cancel leaves name unchanged.\n- Renamed a subdeck (Sub1→Sub2) with \"Deck renamed\" snackbar and persistence; deleted empty decks with Undo/snackbar; expand/collapse arrow toggles expanded state without opening the deck, tapping the row opens the deck, and this held through landscape rotation. Temp subdeck deleted afterwards.\n\n**Browsing & editing cards**\n- Opened/edited note via Edit note: changed Back field, saved, verified persisted; changed then Discarded (\"Discard changes?\"), verified original text; edited again and restored.\n- Verified \"Sort Field\" values match note content; search (`deck:Spanish tag:verb`, `hola`, `mesa`) returns correct counts; tag \"verb\" appears and is the only tag; unchecking/confirming/saving removed it and the tag filter then returned 0; re-adding/saving restored it and the filter returned 1.\n- Noted but not reported (ambiguous expected behavior): after clearing the search box via the X, submitting an empty search leaves the previous filtered results until the search bar is closed.\n\n**Note types**\n- Created temporary note types (deleted after), added/renamed/deleted fields (delete-cancel kept the field; delete confirmed removed it), several position reorders — 1→2, 1→3, 3→1, repeated reorders — order persisted after leaving/re-entering and across rotation, and note field values stayed correctly mapped to their field names after repeated reorders. Sort-field indicator follows its field. Duplicate field rename was silently rejected. Temp note types deleted; Basic field order restored (Front, Back).\n\n**Final state at last successful observation:** only French (3 notes) and Spanish (4 notes) decks, only the \"verb\" tag, Basic note type (7 notes) with original field order and content. I could not complete sign-off because the device connection died."}
